# Dack Fayden, Helping Hand under Weathered Runestone, in a game of three: X is two, so the reveal finds Llanowar Elves and
# then Dryad Arbor. Both are put onto the battlefield, but the Runestone keeps the Elves - a nonland permanent card in a
# library - from entering (CR 101.2), so it stays in the library and is shuffled away; only the Arbor, a land, enters. It
# alone is one of "those permanents": it is goaded, and the one choice of opponent is for it, between both opponents - the
# Elves use none of them up. Bot1 chooses Bot3, who gains control of the goaded Arbor; Bot2 gets nothing. In a game of more
# than two the player who goes first draws on turn 1 (CR 103.8c), so the whole hand is the eight cards cast.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Weathered Runestone
Dack Fayden, Helping Hand
Island
Llanowar Elves
Island
Dryad Arbor
Island x9

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x20

